@scene(20)
// AI geometry tool-use demo — Gate Placement
//
// The part is already posed beside the sprue (longest axis vertical, flattest
// face toward the sprue, 25 mm clearance). Now connect it to the sprue with
// gates. The AI reads the two surfaces with its geometry tools and checks that
// each gate melds into both solids. Open the AI chat and give it this task.
//
// TRY THIS PROMPT:
//   The part is already posed beside the sprue. Add two gates connecting the
//   part to the sprue: one near the TOP of the part and one near the BOTTOM.
//   Name them gateTop and gateBottom, and return piece, sprue, gateTop,
//   gateBottom. Each gate must interpenetrate (meld into) BOTH the part and
//   the sprue — every pairwise max goes negative, which is correct here — and
//   the two gates must not touch each other. A melding solid such as a capsule
//   or cylinder spanning from the part surface to the sprue surface is fine.
//
// What to watch: the model should use extremum to confirm each gate overlaps
// both the part and the sprue (max goes negative), and that the two gates
// stay clear of each other.

boxHalf(half) {
  return max(
    -half.x - p.x, p.x - half.x,
    -half.y - p.y, p.y - half.y,
    -half.z - p.z, p.z - half.z,
  );
}

cylZ(center, radius, halfHeight) {
  q = p - center;
  return max(length(q.xy) - radius, abs(q.z) - halfHeight);
}

piece = remap(boxHalf([10.0, 3.0, 1.5]), [p.z, p.y, p.x + 2.5]);
sprue = cylZ([30.0, 0.0, 0.0], 6.0, 12.0);

return piece, sprue;
